  "findings": [
    "Realistic fictional identities, age-at-arrival, payer, acuity and encounter history are internally consistent across monthly/facility and rare-case contexts. Worker roles, assignment revisions, FTE and credentials remain visible.",
    "Quarterly note review covers pneumonia, COPD, diabetes, chest pain, osteoarthritis and cholecystitis contexts. Narrative facts are grounded to available observations, problems and performed services; full clinical validators independently enforce causal timing and discriminator rules.",
    "Carry-in, continuous-transfer, death, draft original-account and open unbilled contexts remain distinct. Zero claim AR on an unsubmitted draft does not mean zero enterprise/unbilled AR.",
    "The denial and payer calibrations correct misses against original targets without relaxing tolerances. Worker month/day changes preserve birth years and assignment history.",
    "Current primary and comparison-20261024 golden bytes are unchanged by patient-calendar and closed-month projection fixes. The registered third seed retains the formerly failing visit without replacing the seed or dropping proposals.",
    "Selected costs, signed cash, original-account balances and monetary finance-series reconciliations have zero unexplained differences in fresh independent consumers. Final approval still requires all current seed/source/fault/recovery technical gates."
  ],
  "limitations_accepted": true,
  "limitations": [
    "Configured fictional adult pathways and template-driven notes are not population epidemiology, clinical effectiveness or treatment guidance.",
    "Thirty selected late-window terminal outcomes are boundary tests, not a mortality or survival population series. Mortality forecasting is outside this accepted scope.",
    "Selected services, stock and sparse support/admin attendance do not represent complete hospital billing, cost or payroll. Bundled demonstration charges are not a validated reimbursement tariff.",
    "Access grants are a selected revocation-history cohort, not every active authorized user.",
    "The fixed fictional catchment and public name distributions are shared across seeds; additional seeds test connected history sensitivity rather than independent demographic sampling.",
    "Joint-cell Wilson intervals are descriptive within month/facility/class. Repeat visits are correlated; sparse cells receive counts, intervals and domain constraints rather than arbitrary percentage gates or population-inference claims.",
    "Axiom covers twelve illustrative archetypes, with no customer layout/vendor certification and no claim of implementing approximately 900 customer reports. Workday/Axiom interfaces are local source simulations.",
    "Age 100 at the opening baseline may naturally age to 103. Unknown/censored outcomes, missing plans and zero plans remain separate.",
    "Phase 9 clean-environment release certification and explicit final data acceptance are pending. No analytics solution, live integration, forecasting model, dashboard or agent is authorized by this review."
  ],
